# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Public repo for the Multi-Room Alarm Clock integration.
#
# This git repo lives INSIDE a live Home Assistant config folder, which holds
# hundreds of files that are NOT part of this project (secrets, the HA database,
# .storage/ auth tokens, personal dashboards, unrelated integrations, media,
# backups, …). So: deny everything, then explicitly re-include only the paths
# that ship with the published integration.
#
# Pattern: `/*` ignores every entry at the repo root. `!/name` (or `!/name/`)
# re-includes a path; once a directory is re-included, everything inside it is
# tracked. Keep this deny-first structure — do NOT switch to tracking the whole
# config folder.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Deny everything at the repo root by default.
/*

# ── Repo meta ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/LICENSE
!/hacs.json
!/.github/
# screenshots referenced by the README
!/docs/

# ── The integration ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
!/custom_components/
/custom_components/*
!/custom_components/multi_room_alarm/

# ── Lovelace cards that ship with the integration ──────────────────────────
# The reusable alarm cards (row template, list, ringing overlay). Copy the
# whole `dashboards/` folder into your HA config, or cherry-pick.
# Only the shared `alarms/` partials + the generic example are tracked — any
# other dashboard roots you keep in this folder stay untracked.
!/dashboards/
/dashboards/*
!/dashboards/alarms/
!/dashboards/example-room.yaml

# Never track editor / OS cruft even inside re-included folders.
**/.DS_Store
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
